  "scope": "The main standing exhibition buildings of the Ditsong National Museum of Military History in Saxonwold, Johannesburg, including two Bellman halls, attached exhibition ranges and the Masondo Library.",
  "writtenSources": [
    {
      "url": "https://ditsong.org.za/en/our-museums/ditsong-national-museum-of-military-history/",
      "facts": "The museum identifies its Saxonwold site and its opening on 29 August 1947."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://ditsong.org.za/en/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/DMSA-ANNUAL-REPORT-2024-2025.pdf",
      "facts": "The museum operator confirms that the two original Bellman aircraft hangars still house the principal exhibitions and names the F B Adler Hall and G E Brink Hall."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.samilitaryhistory.org/vol105sb.html",
      "facts": "The museum archive records the two hangars erected in 1946, the open space used between them at the opening, and the identification of the former B Hangar with Adler Hall."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://sajournalofarthistory.org.za/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/SAJAH_29_2.pdf",
      "facts": "The field study documents a typical South African Bellman as a wide shallow-gabled corrugated steel frame with large sliding end doors and occasional inserted side windows. It reports a local standard of 28.95 by 38.1 metres and 7.92 metres at the top of the doors. The standard is a section reference, not a measurement of this site."
    }
  ],
